{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:11:32.075143Z","id":"2a364781183f80dffafcb887c47f93e7295f8249254db5206433d81a164a5ffe","body":{"detail":"Since fc43eeb6 the contract's crate docs say billing charges memory at max(memory_bytes, mem_peak_bytes): the Worker sandbox (crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs, ISOLATE_MEMORY_BYTES) reports its isolate's fixed 128 MiB as the peak. Docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 6.1 still says memory is charged at the configured limit; metering arithmetic that reads only Limits::memory_bytes undercharges every Worker run whose limit is under 128 MiB (the default is 64 MiB).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":84},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"ee94befd9f3a34d569280df8d13b2565f8c714f655ddf329e05e4a1f2891cff6"},"suggested_fix":"In clax-bot's metering, charge max(limits.memory_bytes, outcome.mem_peak_bytes) and say so in the spec's section 6.1.","summary":"Billing must charge the larger of Limits::memory_bytes and ScriptOutcome::mem_peak_bytes, which the run driver does not do yet","tags":["claxbot","billing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:35:39.592881Z","id":"4fe98cf9c1981a19391928668dc84633a7f5a7cc8f21b0545a99c7bb00eccb9e","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs (around line 345) singles out only ErrorKind::Unavailable (a stalled wait); every other error kind becomes the step's outcome for the model. InvalidOps is the host's mistake, not the script's: the model cannot fix it by writing another script, and every later script of the run would fail the same way, since the list comes from the run's surfaces. When the run loop starts passing a list (Script::with_ops), it should check the list itself with clax_bot_sandbox::validate_ops before the first step, or treat InvalidOps as ending the run, rather than spend steps on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":594},"end":{"line":597},"content_hash":"d4a9e157566ac22698c212a3ed7484b1940bbf84c4f7d2522207fa13540ab63c"},"summary":"A run whose script carries a list validate_ops refuses ends with ErrorKind::InvalidOps, which crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs treats like any script error: the step fails and the model reads the message","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:35:39.593033Z","id":"b5e2a69175c9e5c279d2a1294813762cf49d4593b31603ced512562e29946d1a","body":{"detail":"clax_surface::Limits (crates/clax-surface/src/limits.rs) bounds one surface: 256 operations, names of 64 bytes, namespaces 32 deep by default and up to MAX_DEPTH 64. The sandbox bounds one script's whole list: 4096 names, 4096 bytes a dotted name, 256 KiB together. Seventeen full surfaces in one run pass 4096 names; a surface read with depth raised to 64 can have a dotted name of 64 + 64 x 65 + 64 bytes, over 4096. Either is refused with ErrorKind::InvalidOps only when a script runs. The sandbox's bounds are what keep the prelude's work and the job's size bounded on their own; the check that a run's surfaces fit them belongs where the run's list is put together, before the run starts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":312},"end":{"line":317},"content_hash":"aa5798dc04e68cd5498f9368fe2cf8d9cb3fcec0e5b0d663c5c8ede931ff01ed"},"summary":"MAX_OPS, MAX_OP_BYTES and MAX_OPS_BYTES are not derived from clax-surface's Limits, so a list made of definitions that each pass crates/clax-surface/src/check.rs can still be refused at run time","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:35:39.593115Z","id":"442354b9424286b2f73c0d978029e68f495090b3f5a19e976fd4df274abd086c","body":{"detail":"With a list, each run copies it: QuickJS into an Arc and a HashSet (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, Sandbox::run) beside the copy Engine's script clone makes, the Worker into RunState's set and the job's JSON. That is at most 256 KiB (MAX_OPS_BYTES) a step, small beside a fresh QuickJS runtime or isolate per step, and nothing for a script without a list. An Arc would need serde's rc feature (a Cargo.toml change and bazel-sync) and a list type the run loop holds as Arc.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"33be7d1932b7b022790a8a7207c307abccebfb038ebb56ce9b3e2e8a9d9367f5"},"summary":"Script::ops as an Arc<[String]> shared by every step of a run, instead of a Vec<String> each step copies","tags":["revisit:a profile of a run step shows copying the operation list matters","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:46:04.141479Z","id":"31088a7a6e01495eeacf342683456ffbe815665fc8cc125eb40b1c217aed6fac","body":{"detail":"Both sandboxes call Host::ask (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/loader.rs), whose default wraps Host::call in HostReply::Answer, so the existing impls (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs StepHost, crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference.rs RunHost, and the test hosts in crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs, crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs and crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs) compile unchanged. Two methods let a host implement both inconsistently: a host overriding ask decides what its call returns for a waiting call (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/conformance.rs ScriptedHost::call turns Waiting into a host error). One method returning HostReply leaves one answer per call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":555},"end":{"line":565},"content_hash":"f9c47b0ff72cd521fe00b6fc0f48a8cd111955b540a27277c4ceb66b47657288"},"summary":"Host::call itself returns HostReply, instead of a provided Host::ask beside it","tags":["revisit:the run loop's StepHost is the only Host outside the sandbox crates and their tests","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:46:44.949558Z","id":"bdc567c5fe2d9df1d655c544b468421c86e0fff3b4b096178b8ff5ddd70278c7","body":{"detail":"Since fc43eeb6 the contract's crate docs say billing charges memory at max(memory_bytes, mem_peak_bytes): the Worker sandbox (crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs, ISOLATE_MEMORY_BYTES) reports its isolate's fixed 128 MiB as the peak. Docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 6.1 still says memory is charged at the configured limit; metering arithmetic that reads only Limits::memory_bytes undercharges every Worker run whose limit is under 128 MiB (the default is 64 MiB).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":111},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"ee94befd9f3a34d569280df8d13b2565f8c714f655ddf329e05e4a1f2891cff6"},"suggested_fix":"In clax-bot's metering, charge max(limits.memory_bytes, outcome.mem_peak_bytes) and say so in the spec's section 6.1.","summary":"Billing must charge the larger of Limits::memory_bytes and ScriptOutcome::mem_peak_bytes, which the run driver does not do yet","supersedes":"2a364781183f80dffafcb887c47f93e7295f8249254db5206433d81a164a5ffe","tags":["claxbot","billing","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:46:45.188417Z","id":"3ccc6148fb7ce41a2aad2d9ffcc5c33f987df570b6730534bfd32fa5f0ce4348","body":{"detail":"With a list, each run copies it: QuickJS into an Arc and a HashSet (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, Sandbox::run) beside the copy Engine's script clone makes, the Worker into RunState's set and the job's JSON. That is at most 256 KiB (MAX_OPS_BYTES) a step, small beside a fresh QuickJS runtime or isolate per step, and nothing for a script without a list. An Arc would need serde's rc feature (a Cargo.toml change and bazel-sync) and a list type the run loop holds as Arc.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"33be7d1932b7b022790a8a7207c307abccebfb038ebb56ce9b3e2e8a9d9367f5"},"summary":"Script::ops as an Arc<[String]> shared by every step of a run, instead of a Vec<String> each step copies","supersedes":"442354b9424286b2f73c0d978029e68f495090b3f5a19e976fd4df274abd086c","tags":["revisit:a profile of a run step shows copying the operation list matters","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:46:45.379338Z","id":"97fa4e012036ea0f98b1766df08e5dfdec89b7053cdb13a7a8ff234cba7c5e80","body":{"detail":"clax_surface::Limits (crates/clax-surface/src/limits.rs) bounds one surface: 256 operations, names of 64 bytes, namespaces 32 deep by default and up to MAX_DEPTH 64. The sandbox bounds one script's whole list: 4096 names, 4096 bytes a dotted name, 256 KiB together. Seventeen full surfaces in one run pass 4096 names; a surface read with depth raised to 64 can have a dotted name of 64 + 64 x 65 + 64 bytes, over 4096. Either is refused with ErrorKind::InvalidOps only when a script runs. The sandbox's bounds are what keep the prelude's work and the job's size bounded on their own; the check that a run's surfaces fit them belongs where the run's list is put together, before the run starts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":337},"content_hash":"aa5798dc04e68cd5498f9368fe2cf8d9cb3fcec0e5b0d663c5c8ede931ff01ed"},"summary":"MAX_OPS, MAX_OP_BYTES and MAX_OPS_BYTES are not derived from clax-surface's Limits, so a list made of definitions that each pass crates/clax-surface/src/check.rs can still be refused at run time","supersedes":"b5e2a69175c9e5c279d2a1294813762cf49d4593b31603ced512562e29946d1a","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:46:45.546518Z","id":"53c6a8a73b624f63e48203f11c590dd03da73feadb21a7eeb084c89eebedcf80","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs (around line 345) singles out only ErrorKind::Unavailable (a stalled wait); every other error kind becomes the step's outcome for the model. InvalidOps is the host's mistake, not the script's: the model cannot fix it by writing another script, and every later script of the run would fail the same way, since the list comes from the run's surfaces. When the run loop starts passing a list (Script::with_ops), it should check the list itself with clax_bot_sandbox::validate_ops before the first step, or treat InvalidOps as ending the run, rather than spend steps on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":635},"end":{"line":638},"content_hash":"d4a9e157566ac22698c212a3ed7484b1940bbf84c4f7d2522207fa13540ab63c"},"summary":"A run whose script carries a list validate_ops refuses ends with ErrorKind::InvalidOps, which crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs treats like any script error: the step fails and the model reads the message","supersedes":"4fe98cf9c1981a19391928668dc84633a7f5a7cc8f21b0545a99c7bb00eccb9e","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T21:35:40.598457Z","id":"f10b2c3b497f2a525ee9fe5f07e04a320f1d03fa4d1b9f2aaf02b064657f581e","body":{"detail":"`Tick::script` (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs) takes the list from `RunSurfaces::operations` (crates/clax-bot/src/registry.rs), checks it with `clax_bot_sandbox::validate_ops` before `begin_step`, and ends the run with `Ending::failed(CODE_OPS_INVALID, …)`; a sandbox that answers `ErrorKind::InvalidOps` all the same (a stricter one) is treated the same after the run, with the sessions dropped. The model is shown no step for it: `generic::a_run_whose_surfaces_operations_are_not_usable_fails_and_takes_no_script_step`. For a run whose one binding is `clax` the list is `clax_bot::api::op_names()` (`generic::a_runs_scripts_are_given_the_operations_of_its_surfaces`).","kind":"comment","references":"53c6a8a73b624f63e48203f11c590dd03da73feadb21a7eeb084c89eebedcf80","summary":"The run loop now passes each script its run's operations and ends the run `failed` (`surface_ops_invalid`) for a list `validate_ops` refuses, before the step is begun","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T22:57:43.869158Z","id":"45b80e72f84d682e4aa8de1d9d11680768123ff3d76d37983ee3a156b9dedc24","body":{"detail":"`then` is refused because `await` calls it. The namespaces of `clax` have no prototype (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js:75), so an operation with one of these names is the only property of that name: `console.log(clax.desk)` and a script's returned value go through `JSON.stringify` (prelude.js:49, 166), which calls `toJSON(\"\")`, and `` `${clax.desk}` `` calls `toString()` then `valueOf()`. Each such call is a call of the host's operation that the script did not write (the run loop still checks its arguments), and for `toString` the coercion then throws a TypeError, since the call's promise is no primitive. `clax_surface` accepts all three as an operation's and as a namespace's name (`callable`, crates/clax-surface/src/allow.rs:47; probed: a host's file with `toJSON(): Promise<null>` reads), and so does `validate_ops`. The JavaScript side is read from prelude.js, not run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":339},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"b4af7771e2d30da65aa488aeb7bcb51c517879c60bb10d97175e0e050751b7f1"},"suggested_fix":"Add `toJSON`, `toString` and `valueOf` to `RESERVED_SEGMENTS`, to the prelude's and the Worker driver's own checks and to `clax_surface`'s `callable`.","summary":"`toJSON`, `toString` and `valueOf` are usable as an operation's name, and are then called by JavaScript itself when a script logs, returns or concatenates the namespace that holds them","tags":["security","review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T23:14:20.943735Z","id":"52ae8d48ccd2e9aac22708ac22a325d94acbca61aa0ddd5c9bd6d5c64564e906","body":{"detail":"The list is `clax_surface::RESERVED_CALLABLE` (crates/clax-surface/src/allow.rs): `__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype`, `then`, `toJSON`, `toString`, `toLocaleString`, `valueOf`, `hasOwnProperty`, `isPrototypeOf`, `propertyIsEnumerable`, `__defineGetter__`, `__defineSetter__`, `__lookupGetter__`, `__lookupSetter__`. `callable` (operations, namespaces, allow patterns) refuses each in both notations for both authors; crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts uses none. `clax_bot_sandbox::RESERVED_SEGMENTS` is the same list (clax-bot-sandbox may not depend on clax-surface; crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs `the_sandbox_reserves_the_names_the_surface_format_does` holds them equal), and src/prelude.js refuses each by a `switch` that the sandbox's own test holds names every one. Tests: crates/clax-surface/src/tests/refusals.rs (a `.d.ts` operation and namespace of each name) and tests/manifest.rs (a manifest operation and namespace of each name); crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/conformance.rs gains twelve `refused_list` cases (`shell.toJSON` … `shell.__lookupSetter__`, `toLocaleString`, `toJSON.read`), run by clax-bot-js and by the Worker's `sandbox_test`. Fields of an interface may still be named so: a value's `toJSON` field is data, not a function, and `JSON.stringify` calls only a function. Left for the owner to close.","kind":"comment","references":"45b80e72f84d682e4aa8de1d9d11680768123ff3d76d37983ee3a156b9dedc24","summary":"Fixed: `toJSON` and the methods of `Object.prototype` are refused beside `then` as an operation's or a namespace's name, by `clax-surface`, `validate_ops` and the prelude, from one list","tags":["security","claxbot-surfaces","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:54:02.022809Z","id":"0033a648dd35f31e8f4f815bf6db3c0f77a5c9a57457002a618ee3e180b02e30","body":{"detail":"`then` is refused because `await` calls it. The namespaces of `clax` have no prototype (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js:75), so an operation with one of these names is the only property of that name: `console.log(clax.desk)` and a script's returned value go through `JSON.stringify` (prelude.js:49, 166), which calls `toJSON(\"\")`, and `` `${clax.desk}` `` calls `toString()` then `valueOf()`. Each such call is a call of the host's operation that the script did not write (the run loop still checks its arguments), and for `toString` the coercion then throws a TypeError, since the call's promise is no primitive. `clax_surface` accepts all three as an operation's and as a namespace's name (`callable`, crates/clax-surface/src/allow.rs:47; probed: a host's file with `toJSON(): Promise<null>` reads), and so does `validate_ops`. The JavaScript side is read from prelude.js, not run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":338},"end":{"line":365},"content_hash":"cd0c3f17d8c0eee8d2a9f290effceb1d2ac5cf505ceb8ad5f1b79fa6be868513"},"suggested_fix":"Add `toJSON`, `toString` and `valueOf` to `RESERVED_SEGMENTS`, to the prelude's and the Worker driver's own checks and to `clax_surface`'s `callable`.","summary":"`toJSON`, `toString` and `valueOf` are usable as an operation's name, and are then called by JavaScript itself when a script logs, returns or concatenates the namespace that holds them","supersedes":"45b80e72f84d682e4aa8de1d9d11680768123ff3d76d37983ee3a156b9dedc24","tags":["security","review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:54:02.320955Z","id":"ad2e5beda061015ebb5013c8225d25d0d8acc05a7cd7d414be69c94013d9fc49","body":{"detail":"Both sandboxes call Host::ask (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/loader.rs), whose default wraps Host::call in HostReply::Answer, so the existing impls (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs StepHost, crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference.rs RunHost, and the test hosts in crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs, crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs and crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs) compile unchanged. Two methods let a host implement both inconsistently: a host overriding ask decides what its call returns for a waiting call (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/conformance.rs ScriptedHost::call turns Waiting into a host error). One method returning HostReply leaves one answer per call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":578},"end":{"line":588},"content_hash":"f9c47b0ff72cd521fe00b6fc0f48a8cd111955b540a27277c4ceb66b47657288"},"summary":"Host::call itself returns HostReply, instead of a provided Host::ask beside it","supersedes":"31088a7a6e01495eeacf342683456ffbe815665fc8cc125eb40b1c217aed6fac","tags":["revisit:the run loop's StepHost is the only Host outside the sandbox crates and their tests","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:54:02.633391Z","id":"f08a77b85891b8d97d98f4b6ce448d247e197981e93c6175fcdda86ce1317a67","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs (around line 345) singles out only ErrorKind::Unavailable (a stalled wait); every other error kind becomes the step's outcome for the model. InvalidOps is the host's mistake, not the script's: the model cannot fix it by writing another script, and every later script of the run would fail the same way, since the list comes from the run's surfaces. When the run loop starts passing a list (Script::with_ops), it should check the list itself with clax_bot_sandbox::validate_ops before the first step, or treat InvalidOps as ending the run, rather than spend steps on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":658},"end":{"line":661},"content_hash":"d4a9e157566ac22698c212a3ed7484b1940bbf84c4f7d2522207fa13540ab63c"},"summary":"A run whose script carries a list validate_ops refuses ends with ErrorKind::InvalidOps, which crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs treats like any script error: the step fails and the model reads the message","supersedes":"53c6a8a73b624f63e48203f11c590dd03da73feadb21a7eeb084c89eebedcf80","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:53:55.085728Z","id":"ec67155bab246e61b3acbd6ec6a67cbca1bcee2f9058d0e4db96074c0a09ff72","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.9 (\"Captured built-ins\"), §17.3 and §18.5 say a script cannot read the capability and that only the prelude makes a Page. Three hooks the script can install reach it:\n\n1. `opFunction` (prelude.js:85-103) serializes `args`, the rest-parameter array, with the captured `JSON.stringify`; JSON.stringify still calls `args.toJSON`, which is `Array.prototype.toJSON` when the script defines it, with `this` = the args array. For every layer call (browser.js:183-185, 200, 202, 206) `args[0]` is the capability. Script: `let leak; Array.prototype.toJSON = function(){ if (typeof this[0] === 'string') leak = this[0]; return this; }; const page = await clax.browser.open(...); await page.goto('/b'); return leak;` returns the capability as the step's value.\n2. `settle` (prelude.js:418-428) resolves the call's promise with the parsed answer, an ordinary object, so resolution reads its `then`: `Object.prototype.then = function(r){ delete Object.prototype.then; leak = this.page; r(this); }` before `clax.browser.open` gets `{page: <capability>, ...}`; calling `r({page: 'any string', url})` instead makes `pageOf` (browser.js:240, 302) build a Page of that string, which `stateHooks.encode` (browser.js:265-280) then writes into the step's `handles`.\n3. `await flat.open(...)` (browser.js:301) reads `Promise.prototype.constructor`; a script that redefines it and `Promise.prototype.then` receives the resolved `{page}` the same way.\n\nAll three were run against the spliced prelude (`prelude_source(true)` text, prelude.js + browser.js) in a fresh V8 realm with a fake host answering `browser.open` with `{page: \"SECRET-CAP\"}`: each script returned \"SECRET-CAP\", and the second's committed `handles` held `{\"page\": \"FORGED\"}`. QuickJS follows the same specification steps (SerializeJSONProperty reads toJSON on objects; promise resolution reads `then`).\n\nWhat bounds it: `BrowserSessions::verified` (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs:563-575) and `close_unheld` (live.rs:481-505) accept a capability only when its run is the session's and its holder caveat admits the calling run, and `Keys::root`/`child` (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/cap.rs:494-509) always carry `holder=run:<R>`, so neither a leaked nor a forged string drives another run's session or keeps one open. The capability still reaches the model, the step's stored `value`/`logs` the run panel shows (crates/clax-server/src/routes/bot.rs:1767-1768), and anything the model writes, which §18.5 marks as the owner's rule; it will matter more once §18.5's channels to other runs and grant holders exist.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"254cf03d7875a44f129cd30a747786fc28bebe9ae722f9fee7c2f72b8a96fa80"},"suggested_fix":"Give the layer a private channel that no prototype is consulted on: (a) serialize call arguments from a null-prototype array (`setPrototypeOf(args, null)` on the rest array, or build the array the layer sends with `plain()`), and (b) for the five browser session operations, keep the parsed answer in a closure-held record keyed by call ID and resolve the promise with `undefined` (or a null-prototype box read through a WeakMap), the layer reading the answer from that record after the await, so neither `Object.prototype.then`, `Promise.prototype.then` nor `constructor` sees it. Add conformance cases in crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/conformance.rs for each of the three hooks, asserting the returned value and logs never hold the answered `page` and that the handle entry's `page` is the answered one.","summary":"A script reads a Page's serialized capability, and can make a Page name any string, through Array.prototype.toJSON, Object.prototype.then or Promise.prototype.then/constructor, which the prelude's host calls still consult after the script starts","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:53:55.085881Z","id":"e0deaa5a462aa589e3ac6ee8ae842fda879087959f454e97aa62900cd1f397b1","body":{"detail":"Failure: a script that returns normally after `state.page = page; state.note = '\\u{1F600}x'.slice(0, 1);` (any string in state cut inside a surrogate pair, such as page text with an emoji truncated by `slice`) commits no state, tells the model nothing, and its new page is closed `dropped`.\n\nThe prelude's `saveState` (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js:209-211, 281-288) keeps strings as they are and serializes them with JSON.stringify, which writes a lone surrogate as the escape `\"\\ud83d\"` (well-formed JSON.stringify; checked in V8). `StateOut::read` (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs:818-821) parses that with `serde_json::from_str`, which refuses an unpaired surrogate escape when it reads a string (serde_json 1.0.151, src/read.rs `parse_unicode_escape`: `LoneLeadingSurrogateInHexEscape` / `UnexpectedEndOfHexEscape`) and so answers `None`, on both sandboxes (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs:736; crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs:701-706). In crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs:704-713 an outcome without error gives `stopped = None`, so `state::fit(None, None)` (crates/clax-bot/src/state.rs:121-131) answers `saved: None, told: None`: the last committed state stands, the result has no `state` field, and `close_unheld` closes every session only this script's state held. Spec §17.1 says what cannot be kept is reported, never dropped silently (owner). Logs already handle this case (prelude.js:49-66 `wellFormed`, lib.rs module docs \"Logs\"), the state encoding does not; the returned value does not either, but there a parse failure is at least reported (clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs:748-753).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":818},"end":{"line":821},"content_hash":"9a19e33cde0edf8ef0fa8b120c77343fa988e3ae23007031a21ba5bd312b6bc5"},"suggested_fix":"In `saveState`'s `enc`, pass each kept string and each member name through the captured `wellFormed` (lone surrogates to U+FFFD, as `toText` does), so the encoded state always parses; and in script.rs treat a `done` that carried state text `StateOut::read` refused as not saved, with a `told` of `{\"saved\": false, \"why\": ...}`, instead of saying nothing. Add a conformance case (a string with a lone surrogate in `state`) and a run-loop case in crates/clax-bot/tests/state.rs.","summary":"A state holding a string with an unpaired UTF-16 surrogate is lost silently: the prelude writes it as a \\uD8xx escape, StateOut::read's serde_json refuses that, and the step stores and tells nothing","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:53:55.086823Z","id":"1c4e6ff208329a6e4d5b55b739707a3aa6fbbd4a4ace093e77ebc356f93b29b7","body":{"detail":"In `saveState`'s `enc`, the member read `x[k[i]]` (prelude.js:268) sits inside the `try` of the enclosing object's own call (prelude.js:247-276), so its throw is caught there: the object holding the getter is dropped with that object's path, and every sibling member with it. For a getter defined directly on `state` (`Object.defineProperty(state, 'g', {get(){ throw 1 }, enumerable: true})`), `enc(current, \"state\", 0)` returns `undefined`, `value` becomes `{}` (prelude.js:281-282), and the result lists only `{\"path\": \"state\", \"why\": \"reading it threw\"}`; run against the spliced prelude in V8, a state `{a: 1, page: <Page>}` with such a getter came back `{\"value\": {}, ...}`, so at commit `close_unheld` (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs:481-505) closes the page `dropped`. Likewise `state.a = {x: 1}` with a throwing getter on `state.a` loses `state.a.x`. Spec §17.1 lists \"a getter that throws\" among the values each \"left out ... and listed with its path\"; the conformance case `what_state_cannot_keep_is_listed_with_its_path` (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/conformance.rs:1430-1460) pins the parent-wide drop (`state.g` for a getter `state.g.boom`) and has no case with siblings or a getter on `state` itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":247},"end":{"line":276},"content_hash":"8fbd8d98e6d19090de0fa799cc58841b44942ab189f315dce486e7ad2a1cc739"},"suggested_fix":"Read each member in its own `try` (`let m; try { m = x[k[i]]; } catch (_) { drop(at, \"reading it threw\"); continue; }`, and the same for array items), keeping the outer `try` only for `keys`/`getPrototypeOf` traps; update the conformance case to expect `state.g.boom` and add one with a throwing getter on `state` beside a kept member.","summary":"One getter that throws leaves out the whole object holding it, not the member: a throwing getter on `state` itself drops the entire state and closes every page in it","tags":["review","review:browser-unify","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:57:03.003294Z","id":"a60d0c7d82181474ccc53fb54e86298d0c30ce9ba3bed1dfae9802f5ec73dc1f","body":{"detail":"Traced: opFunction's rest array `args` (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js:85-93) has Array.prototype, so the captured `stringify(args)` still reads `args.toJSON`; `settle` (prelude.js:418-424) resolves with `parse(json)`, an ordinary object whose `then` resolution reads; `open` (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/browser.js:300-303) awaits a native promise, and `await` calls PromiseResolve, which reads `.constructor` and, when it is not %Promise%, wraps it and calls the script's `Promise.prototype.then`. Run in node 26 (V8): prelude.js with browser.js spliced at its `  // browser-layer` line (as prelude_source(true), crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs:985-995), lockdown applied, a fake host answering browser.open with {page:\"SECRET-CAP\"}. Output: `toJSON {\"ok\":true,\"payload\":\"\\\"SECRET-CAP\\\"\"...}`, `objthen {\"ok\":true,\"payload\":\"\\\"SECRET-CAP\\\"\"...}`, `forge ... \"handles\":[{\"page\":\"FORGED\",\"url\":\"u\",\"of\":\"Page\"}]`, and, with Promise.prototype.constructor redefined plus Promise.prototype.then wrapped, `promctor2 {\"ok\":true,\"payload\":\"\\\"SECRET-CAP\\\"\"...}` (redefining `then` alone, without `constructor`, leaked nothing). The bound holds: BrowserSessions::verified (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs:563-575) and close_unheld (live.rs:482-505) require `c.run() == e.run` and `c.admits(&Holder::Run(run))`, and Keys::root (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/cap.rs:494-498) always adds the holder caveat, so a leaked or forged string drives no other run's session; it is exposure of the capability, not cross-run control, so concern.","kind":"comment","references":"ec67155bab246e61b3acbd6ec6a67cbca1bcee2f9058d0e4db96074c0a09ff72","summary":"confirmed: all three prototype hooks read the capability, and Object.prototype.then forges a Page that state encodes; concern is the right kind","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:57:03.004974Z","id":"c1cf4e958e5d0250c17eec2cf5f68457f41c8a9d04a2fb690936e54bc97f2d65","body":{"detail":"Prelude side, run in node 26 (V8) against prelude.js: `state.note = '\\u{1F600}x'.slice(0, 1)` gives saved text `{\"value\":{\"note\":\"\\ud83d\"},...}` (enc at crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js:211 returns strings as they are; line 288 stringifies). Rust side: StateOut::read (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs:818-821) is `serde_json::from_str(text?).ok()?`; Cargo.lock pins serde_json 1.0.151, whose str path calls `parse_str_bytes(scratch, true, as_str)` (src/read.rs:336, 588) and with validate=true parse_unicode_escape errors LoneLeadingSurrogateInHexEscape / UnexpectedEndOfHexEscape (src/read.rs:900-960). Both sandboxes call it on done's state (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs:736; crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs:701-703). In crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs:704-713 a normal end gives stopped=None, so state::fit(None, None) (crates/clax-bot/src/state.rs:121-130) returns saved None, told None; script.rs:736-743 then commits `start` (the previous state) and computes `held` from it, so a page opened this step and kept only in state is not held and close_unheld (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/provider.rs:280) closes it dropped. Nothing tells the model, against spec §17.1 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md:1609). Truncated page text with an emoji is an ordinary input, so the blocker's Failure is one a user would hit.","kind":"comment","references":"e0deaa5a462aa589e3ac6ee8ae842fda879087959f454e97aa62900cd1f397b1","summary":"confirmed: a lone surrogate in state makes StateOut::read answer None, the step keeps the old state silently, and its new pages close","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T05:57:03.009175Z","id":"1bae1755003713ed2fa8301492894653acd5569d520864647d13f09dcd0f0891","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js:268 evaluates `x[k[i]]` before calling enc, inside the try at prelude.js:247-276, whose catch (274-276) drops `path` (the holder) and returns undefined. Run in node 26 (V8) against prelude.js with browser.js spliced, a state `{a: 1, page: <Page>}` plus `Object.defineProperty(state, 'g', {get(){ throw 1 }, enumerable: true})` saved `{\"value\":{},...,\"dropped\":[{\"path\":\"state\",\"why\":\"reading it threw\"}]}`: `a` and `page` are gone, so the committed state holds no page and close_unheld (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs:482-505) closes it. `state.a = {x: 1}` with a throwing getter on `state.a` saved `{\"value\":{\"b\":2},...,\"dropped\":[{\"path\":\"state.a\",...}]}`, losing state.a.x. Spec §17.1 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md:1609) lists \"a getter that throws\" as a value left out on its own; conformance case what_state_cannot_keep_is_listed_with_its_path (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/conformance.rs:1432-1460) expects `state.g` for a getter on `state.g.boom`, pinning the holder-wide drop. Needs a script that defines a throwing getter, so concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"1c4e6ff208329a6e4d5b55b739707a3aa6fbbd4a4ace093e77ebc356f93b29b7","summary":"confirmed: the getter is read as the argument of the inner enc call, inside the enclosing object's try, so the whole object and its siblings are dropped","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:35:24.980997Z","id":"14b4d523399e242966b531264252a3ac0db88616c2a0f884e14d5812e6a5dc8e","body":{"detail":"With a list, each run copies it: QuickJS into an Arc and a HashSet (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, Sandbox::run) beside the copy Engine's script clone makes, the Worker into RunState's set and the job's JSON. That is at most 256 KiB (MAX_OPS_BYTES) a step, small beside a fresh QuickJS runtime or isolate per step, and nothing for a script without a list. An Arc would need serde's rc feature (a Cargo.toml change and bazel-sync) and a list type the run loop holds as Arc.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":168},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"33be7d1932b7b022790a8a7207c307abccebfb038ebb56ce9b3e2e8a9d9367f5"},"summary":"Script::ops as an Arc<[String]> shared by every step of a run, instead of a Vec<String> each step copies","supersedes":"3ccc6148fb7ce41a2aad2d9ffcc5c33f987df570b6730534bfd32fa5f0ce4348","tags":["revisit:a profile of a run step shows copying the operation list matters","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:35:25.211818Z","id":"00f71932d89ccd44d2c7c63c3f96c46122e6febe1fc90b1508e988bbbf006b75","body":{"detail":"clax_surface::Limits (crates/clax-surface/src/limits.rs) bounds one surface: 256 operations, names of 64 bytes, namespaces 32 deep by default and up to MAX_DEPTH 64. The sandbox bounds one script's whole list: 4096 names, 4096 bytes a dotted name, 256 KiB together. Seventeen full surfaces in one run pass 4096 names; a surface read with depth raised to 64 can have a dotted name of 64 + 64 x 65 + 64 bytes, over 4096. Either is refused with ErrorKind::InvalidOps only when a script runs. The sandbox's bounds are what keep the prelude's work and the job's size bounded on their own; the check that a run's surfaces fit them belongs where the run's list is put together, before the run starts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":378},"end":{"line":383},"content_hash":"aa5798dc04e68cd5498f9368fe2cf8d9cb3fcec0e5b0d663c5c8ede931ff01ed"},"summary":"MAX_OPS, MAX_OP_BYTES and MAX_OPS_BYTES are not derived from clax-surface's Limits, so a list made of definitions that each pass crates/clax-surface/src/check.rs can still be refused at run time","supersedes":"97fa4e012036ea0f98b1766df08e5dfdec89b7053cdb13a7a8ff234cba7c5e80","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:35:25.436630Z","id":"32fdc4a91fe6c17a99e5af92d368d8a461e30647d00703f838829b5b7ff917c4","body":{"detail":"`then` is refused because `await` calls it. The namespaces of `clax` have no prototype (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js:75), so an operation with one of these names is the only property of that name: `console.log(clax.desk)` and a script's returned value go through `JSON.stringify` (prelude.js:49, 166), which calls `toJSON(\"\")`, and `` `${clax.desk}` `` calls `toString()` then `valueOf()`. Each such call is a call of the host's operation that the script did not write (the run loop still checks its arguments), and for `toString` the coercion then throws a TypeError, since the call's promise is no primitive. `clax_surface` accepts all three as an operation's and as a namespace's name (`callable`, crates/clax-surface/src/allow.rs:47; probed: a host's file with `toJSON(): Promise<null>` reads), and so does `validate_ops`. The JavaScript side is read from prelude.js, not run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":384},"end":{"line":411},"content_hash":"cd0c3f17d8c0eee8d2a9f290effceb1d2ac5cf505ceb8ad5f1b79fa6be868513"},"suggested_fix":"Add `toJSON`, `toString` and `valueOf` to `RESERVED_SEGMENTS`, to the prelude's and the Worker driver's own checks and to `clax_surface`'s `callable`.","summary":"`toJSON`, `toString` and `valueOf` are usable as an operation's name, and are then called by JavaScript itself when a script logs, returns or concatenates the namespace that holds them","supersedes":"0033a648dd35f31e8f4f815bf6db3c0f77a5c9a57457002a618ee3e180b02e30","tags":["security","review","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:35:25.658415Z","id":"72bae14a2087ce275be7f4f0e312871a412dd8e4fe73584d4754a38ce4ff78a8","body":{"detail":"Both sandboxes call Host::ask (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/loader.rs), whose default wraps Host::call in HostReply::Answer, so the existing impls (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs StepHost, crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference.rs RunHost, and the test hosts in crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs, crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs and crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs) compile unchanged. Two methods let a host implement both inconsistently: a host overriding ask decides what its call returns for a waiting call (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/conformance.rs ScriptedHost::call turns Waiting into a host error). One method returning HostReply leaves one answer per call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":641},"end":{"line":651},"content_hash":"f9c47b0ff72cd521fe00b6fc0f48a8cd111955b540a27277c4ceb66b47657288"},"summary":"Host::call itself returns HostReply, instead of a provided Host::ask beside it","supersedes":"ad2e5beda061015ebb5013c8225d25d0d8acc05a7cd7d414be69c94013d9fc49","tags":["revisit:the run loop's StepHost is the only Host outside the sandbox crates and their tests","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:35:25.878346Z","id":"0d8992c0f7830acb02390f38628f2e3e5494634c6ae3c5355bdede8de6aba463","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs (around line 345) singles out only ErrorKind::Unavailable (a stalled wait); every other error kind becomes the step's outcome for the model. InvalidOps is the host's mistake, not the script's: the model cannot fix it by writing another script, and every later script of the run would fail the same way, since the list comes from the run's surfaces. When the run loop starts passing a list (Script::with_ops), it should check the list itself with clax_bot_sandbox::validate_ops before the first step, or treat InvalidOps as ending the run, rather than spend steps on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":721},"end":{"line":724},"content_hash":"d4a9e157566ac22698c212a3ed7484b1940bbf84c4f7d2522207fa13540ab63c"},"summary":"A run whose script carries a list validate_ops refuses ends with ErrorKind::InvalidOps, which crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs treats like any script error: the step fails and the model reads the message","supersedes":"f08a77b85891b8d97d98f4b6ce448d247e197981e93c6175fcdda86ce1317a67","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T16:39:14.198963Z","id":"f425a3b602fa78cd42da50f581b957820c69785af001f40efff43e83541891e5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0920734ee499","summary":"Fixed in 0920734ee: saveState makes strings, member names and paths well-formed; a state text that does not read is told {saved: false, why}. Evidence: conformance a_lone_surrogate_in_state_is_kept_well_formed, state::a_lone_surrogate_in_state_is_kept_well_formed, a_state_text_that_does_not_read_says_why, which failed on the code before the fix, passes in //crates/clax-bot-js:integration, //crates/clax-bot:integration, //crates/clax-worker:sandbox_test; `PATH=~/.local/homebrew/bin:$PATH just check` at 45cd24c07 printed 'Executed 85 out of 407 tests: 407 tests pass.' and 'bazel: all checks passed'","supersedes":"e0deaa5a462aa589e3ac6ee8ae842fda879087959f454e97aa62900cd1f397b1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T16:39:14.424913Z","id":"db3494ee9416ea7053120e03956df513a025f2d171219f44b6e46826d9f6f494","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c093592f93f1","summary":"Fixed in c093592f9: each member and array item is read in its own try. Evidence: conformance a_getter_that_throws_leaves_out_only_its_member, which failed on the code before the fix, passes in //crates/clax-bot-js:integration, //crates/clax-worker:sandbox_test; `PATH=~/.local/homebrew/bin:$PATH just check` at 45cd24c07 printed 'Executed 85 out of 407 tests: 407 tests pass.' and 'bazel: all checks passed'","supersedes":"1c4e6ff208329a6e4d5b55b739707a3aa6fbbd4a4ace093e77ebc356f93b29b7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-20T16:39:14.652651Z","id":"6a825b79abd1fc8cf65d333d6e77a19b085b26335f76d0dbac076cad95597fd0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:236a6b24e59a","summary":"Fixed in 236a6b24e: host calls send their arguments from a null-prototype array; the layer's session calls get their answers through a record only the layer holds and resolve undefined. Each case leaked or forged before the fix. Evidence: conformance array_to_json_sees_no_capability, object_then_sees_no_answer_and_forges_no_page, promise_then_and_constructor_see_no_answer, which failed on the code before the fix, passes in //crates/clax-bot-js:integration, //crates/clax-worker:sandbox_test; `PATH=~/.local/homebrew/bin:$PATH just check` at 45cd24c07 printed 'Executed 85 out of 407 tests: 407 tests pass.' and 'bazel: all checks passed'","supersedes":"ec67155bab246e61b3acbd6ec6a67cbca1bcee2f9058d0e4db96074c0a09ff72","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
